# 📘 Bookmark Link Checker

![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.10%2B-blue)
![Status](https://img.shields.io/badge/status-active-success)
![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-green)
![Concurrency](https://img.shields.io/badge/concurrency-multithreaded-orange)
![Resilience](https://img.shields.io/badge/retry-backoff%20%2B%20jitter-blueviolet)

A Python tool for analyzing, cleaning, and validating large Chrome bookmark collections.

It parses exported bookmarks, removes duplicates, checks links in parallel with retry and politeness controls,
and generates clean, importable outputs—including one that preserves your original folder structure without
broken links.

---

## 🚀 What this solves

If you’ve ever had thousands of bookmarks, you already know:

- Some are dead 💀
- Some redirect somewhere unexpected
- Some are duplicates
- And finding anything useful becomes painful

This tool turns that chaos into something usable again.

---

## ⚡ Quick Example

```bash
python -m bookmark_checker.main \
  --bookmarks bookmarks.html \
  --out results.csv \
  --workers 10 \
  --dedupe-mode aggressive


## 🏗 Architecture Overview

```mermaid



bookmark_checker/
│
├── main.py                     # Orchestration + pipeline
│
├── models.py                   # Bookmark, CheckResult
├── parse_bookmarks.py          # HTML parsing
├── dedupe.py                   # Deduplication logic
├── normalize.py                # URL normalization
│
├── checks/
│   ├── http_check.py           # Single request logic (no retries)
│   ├── retry.py                # Retry + backoff wrapper
│   └── politeness.py           # Per-domain throttling
│
├── writers/
│   └── folder_preserving.py    # Rebuilds original folder structure
│
├── utils/
│   ├── dates.py
│   ├── logging.py
│   └── paths.py
│
└── config.py                   # Defaults + config loading


Some Features
🔍 Bookmark Processing
    Parses Chrome bookmark HTML exports
    Supports nested folder structures
    Preserves metadata like title and add date

🧹 Deduplication
Multiple modes:
    strict
    basic
    tracking_free
    aggressive
    Normalizes URLs before comparison
    Removes duplicates safely

⚡ Parallel Link Checking
    Multi-threaded (ThreadPoolExecutor)
    Per-thread HTTP sessions (connection reuse)
    Configurable worker count
⏳ Politeness Controls
    Per-domain delay to avoid hammering servers
    Shared throttling across threads
🔁 Retry & Backoff
    Automatic retry for transient failures
    Exponential backoff + jitter
    Clean separation between:
    "check once" logic
    retry wrapper
🧠 Smart Failure Detection
    Detects:
        HTTP errors
        soft 404s
        potential login walls
        content-based failures

📤 Outputs

After processing, the tool generates:

📄 CSV (Full Results)

Detailed record of every checked URL:
    status
    final URL
    error type
    retry history